From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: consume an empty packet

The Blu-ray 3D demuxer (CDemuxStreamSSIF) hands the player an empty packet,
no data and no timestamp, whenever it has no base/MVC pair to give: while it
waits for one, and for every base picture it drops because the second view
starts later. A resume of a 3D Blu-ray sends dozens before the first pair.

CAMLCodec::AddData refuses a packet without data, so the wrapper returned
false; the video thread then puts the packet back at the head of its queue
and retries it, about every millisecond, with every real packet behind it.
The decoder never opened: no picture, audio on its own, "video decoder
returned error" without end. Mid-film the same packet would freeze the
picture.

An empty packet is now consumed, as the FFmpeg codec does
(CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::AddData). Since 18_01 every 3D Blu-ray goes through
the MVC demuxer on a display that can show it, 2D playback included.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
index 0bab531..6f60cd8 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
@@ -620,6 +620,11 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecAmlogic::AddData(const DemuxPacket &packet)
 {
   m_seekPreroll.SetDrop((m_codecControlFlags & DVD_CODEC_CTRL_DROP) != 0);
 
+  // an empty packet (the Blu-ray 3D demuxer's while it waits for a view pair)
+  // carries nothing: refused, it would be retried ahead of every later packet
+  if (!packet.pData || packet.iSize <= 0)
+    return true;
+
   // Handle Input, add demuxer packet to input queue, we must accept it or
   // it will be discarded as VideoPlayerVideo has no concept of "try again".
 
